    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.5.06-04",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The notch should be located against the cliff at the stated level of wave action, not arbitrarily at the top. It is a local recess, distinct from a cave extending into a headland. If the figure shows a wider recess stretching along the foot, describe that form accurately. Tides and changing water levels mean that effective attack can occur over a vertical zone rather than one permanent line. Do not infer a fixed height above a datum unless the resource provides it. The scale of a notch and the height of the whole cliff are separate measurements.",
