    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.5.06-06",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "An original cross-section can show an earlier cliff line seaward of the present line, a notch at the present foot and a low rock surface between them. The relative positions support cliff retreat and platform development. If the horizontal distance between dated cliff lines is supplied, it can support an average retreat estimate for that interval. A stylised drawing without a scale cannot establish metres of retreat, and a platform’s present width need not equal the distance removed during one recent event. Its history can extend over many episodes and changing conditions.",
