    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.5.06-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "When an arch roof collapses, an isolated pillar of rock may remain offshore as a stack. The stack is separated from the mainland; that separation is part of the identifying relationship. The fallen roof material can become debris that is later moved or worn. Do not skip directly from cave to stack without explaining the formation and loss of the connecting roof if the task asks for the full sequence. A stack may remain for a long period or be reduced relatively quickly under suitable conditions; one sequence diagram does not establish its lifetime.",
