    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.5.06-13",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Continued erosion and weathering can reduce a stack to a lower remnant called a stump. A stump may be more visible at low water and partly or wholly submerged at other stages. It is not simply the shadow of a tall stack or a separate pile of recently deposited sand. In a resource sequence, compare the height and continuity of the rock remnant and read the water-level reference. If the final frame shows a low rock base where a taller isolated pillar previously stood, the change supports reduction from stack to stump.",
