    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.5.06-15",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "An original four-frame resource can label A as a joint opening into a headland, B as an enlarged chamber, C as a passage beneath a surviving roof and D as a detached pillar after roof collapse. A and B show weakness enlargement and cave development, C an arch and D a stack. If a further frame shows a much lower rock base, it can represent a stump. The description should not infer that frames occupy equal time intervals unless dates are given. A labelled letter indicates the order supplied, not a measured duration.\n\n![Cave, arch, stack and stump on one headland, from the sea and in plan](../../assets/images/ITEM-6137-1.5-020-INTERP-answer.png)",
