    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.5.06-17",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Scale also matters. A small crack can be a weakness from which a cave develops, but it is not already a large cave simply because a later drawing shows one. A rock pillar separated by a narrow gap is still distinct from a connected arch if no roof joins it to the mainland. A measured platform width, cliff height and cave depth have different reference directions. Keep their units and labels attached to the correct feature. This is particularly useful when interpreting a resource that places several measurements close together.",
