    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.5.06-19",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A complete account links the form, mechanism and evidence. For a cliff and platform, explain base erosion, support loss, retreat and the remaining rock surface. For a headland sequence, explain the weakness, cave enlargement, arch breakthrough, roof collapse and later reduction where shown. For headlands and bays, compare resistance and relative retreat. The same erosion vocabulary appears in each explanation, but its role is different. Listing hydraulic action and abrasion without describing what they do in the particular sequence leaves the landform formation unexplained.",
