    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.5.06-20",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A scaled original cliff resource can separate the relationships further. The cliff is 18 m high, the notch extends 2 m horizontally into its foot and the exposed rock platform is 30 m wide at the stated low-water stage. These values describe three different dimensions. The notch depth does not equal cliff retreat for the whole observation period, and platform width is not cliff height. If the next dated survey places the cliff line 3 m landward, that gives an additional horizontal change, not a reason to subtract 3 m from its height. A description should attach each number to its feature and direction before using it in an explanation.",
